      "id": "skip-the-perfect-setup",
      "title": "Skip the perfect setup",
      "minutes": 2,
      "theme_label": "waiting to start",
      "body": "Waiting for the perfect setup is a polite form of delay. The right playlist, tidy desk, ideal mood — useful sometimes, costly when they become entry fees for starting.\n\nSkip the perfect setup and begin in the conditions you have. Two messy minutes beat another hour of arranging. Momentum teaches better than readiness fantasies.\n\nProfessionals start cold often. Warmth arrives after contact with the work, not before. Let action create the state you were waiting to feel.\n\nKeep tools simple. Reduce the runway. Make the first step embarrassingly small so resistance has less to argue with.\n\nToday, begin one postponed thing without upgrading the environment first. Start ugly; refine later.\n\nMomentum teaches better than readiness fantasies. Start ugly if you must; refine later. Contact with the work creates the state you were waiting to feel.",
