      "id": "celebrate-tiny-finishes",
      "title": "Celebrate tiny finishes",
      "minutes": 2,
      "theme_label": "micro-completion",
      "body": "Tiny finishes teach your brain that progress is real. A sent email, a washed mug, a walked block — celebrated briefly — builds motivation better than waiting for a rare big win.\n\nMicro-completion counters the fog of endless projects. When everything is mid-stream, morale drops. Closing small loops restores a sense of agency.\n\nKeep the celebration honest and light: a checkmark, a stretch, a quiet “done.” You are not performing for an audience. You are marking reality.\n\nString enough tiny finishes together and larger goals stop feeling mythical. Momentum prefers evidence.\n\nToday, choose three small closable things and finish them on purpose. Notice the shift in your shoulders when something actually ends.\n\nString enough tiny finishes together and larger goals stop feeling mythical. Momentum prefers evidence — give your brain some today.",
