      "id": "soften-your-shoulders-now",
      "title": "Soften your shoulders now",
      "minutes": 2,
      "theme_label": "body tension",
      "body": "Shoulders rise without permission — at desks, in cars, in tense chats. Softening them now is a direct message to your nervous system that the tiger is not in the room.\n\nBody tension is information. Releasing it does not deny stress; it stops stress from becoming your default posture. Drop shoulders, unclench tongue from the roof of the mouth, ease the hands.\n\nSet a few cues today: doorway = soften; send button = soften; kettle = soften. Pair ordinary moments with a release.\n\nA softer body thinks more clearly. This is practical, not mystical.\n\nRight now, and once more later, soften your shoulders on purpose.\n\nA softer body thinks more clearly. Pair ordinary cues — doorway, kettle, send — with a release so calm becomes a worn path.",
      "practice": "Drop your shoulders, unclench your jaw, and take two breaths. Repeat whenever you notice tension today.",
